{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35788-essential-wraith-books","id":35788,"title":"Essential Wraith Books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T13:50:21-08:00","id":35788,"title":"Essential Wraith Books?","content":"With the DriveThruRPG sale on Wraith, I've decided to dive in and snag a handful of pdfs. I know the book on the Shadow is fantastic, but beyond that I have no clue what to purchase. Any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T14:40:48-08:00","id":35815,"title":"","content":"All of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay, for real, essentials - Sea of Shadows, Player's Guide, Shadow Player's Guide, Book of Legions, Ends of Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T14:43:47-08:00","id":35819,"title":"","content":"My top five:<br /> <br /> Wraith: the Great War<br /> Book of Legions<br /> Doomslayers<br /> Dark Reflections Spectres<br /> Charnel Houses of Europe<br /> <br /> I also got a lot of use out of Mediums and Risen, but in my Vampire game more than my Wraith game.<br /> <br /> I also strongly recommend Orpheus, which is also on sale this week and one of my favorite World of Darkness books.<br /> <br /> -MMM<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T16:44:02-08:00","id":35908,"title":"","content":"Well if you can't afford the bundle, which I highly recommend, I'd say get the following:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/42/Book-of-Legions?cPath=1_43&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Legions</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/105/Dark-Reflections-Spectres?cPath=1_43&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Reflections Spectres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/117/Doomslayers-Into-the-Labyrinth?cPath=1_43&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/258/Sea-of-Shadows?cPath=1_43&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Sea of Shadows</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/349/Wraith-Players-Guide?cPath=1_43&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Wraith Player's Guide</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/259/Shadow-Players-Guide?cPath=1_43&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Shadow Player's Guide</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/155/The-Hierarchy?cPath=1_43&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">The Hierarchy</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/123/Ends-of-Empire?cPath=1_43&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ends of Empire</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/58/Charnel-Houses-of-Europe-The-Shoah?cPath=1_43&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Charnel Houses of Europe</a><br /> <br /> I'd also say the Guild Books and Wraith the Great War too if you can afford them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T17:36:59-08:00","id":35945,"title":"","content":"Ends of Empire and Sea of Shadows is definitely worth it. Even if you get the softcover black and white of Ends of Empire because finding the supplement book itself is so rare the auctions tend to run nearly 100 dollars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:18:11-08:00","id":36135,"title":"","content":"<i>Ends of Empire</i> and <i>Charnel Houses of Europe</i> will blow your mind.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T12:42:45-08:00","id":370015,"title":"","content":"Besides the core 2nd-ed book and its errata (free! ...and necessary for regaining Pathos), I think the essentials are:<br /> 1. Guildbook: Masquers - important clarifications on the nature of corpus<br /> 2. Dark Reflections: Spectres - there isn't much specific info on these guys in the core book<br /> <br /> Also useful if the campaign continues for a while:<br /> * Guildbook: Sandmen - if you want Phantasm to make more sense<br /> * Sea of Shadows - if you want to go adventuring in the Tempest<br /> * Shadow Player's Guide<br /> * Book of Legions - of all the factions, the Hierarchy is the one you cannot avoid, so here's a boatload of GM material<br /> <br /> Charnel Houses, Doomslayers, Great War, and the shadowlands-around-the-world material in the Players Guide are all really cool, but I wouldn't say essential for play. (I have not read Ends of Empire.)<br /> <br /> If you're playing a crossover game instead of a real wraith game, just get The Risen and play one of those. That's about it. Maybe Mediums too, if ghosts are a real theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}